       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 10,000 mg three times daily is 30 g/day, which is about 7 times the usual maximum of 4 g/day for an adult. A single 10 g dose is already in the range that can cause serious hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function. At 70 kg, 10 g is about 143 mg/kg, which is above the toxic threshold of roughly 150 mg/kg when repeated.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3 g/day), a common standard regimen\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours**, or **500 mg PO every 6 hours**\n- **1000 mg PO four times daily** (4 g/day, the maximum). The order system only takes whole-number frequencies, so a four-times-daily order would be 4.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If 10,000 mg three times daily is what you intended, tell me the clinical reason. I'd still want to confirm it before entering something like that."
