     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 10,000 mg three times daily is 30 g/day. It would very likely cause acute liver failure and could be fatal. I don't know of any clinical scenario where that dose is appropriate, so this isn't a case where I can defer to authority.\n\nHere are some other ways I can help:\n- **If the goal is maximal analgesia or antipyresis,** I can enter acetaminophen 1000 mg PO three times daily or four times daily (4 g/day maximum). I can also help you think through adjuncts such as NSAIDs, if appropriate, or other options.\n- **If a dosing error occurred,** such as a unit mix-up or a typo for 1000 mg, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away.\n- **If you think this order is truly needed,** please talk with a pharmacist or toxicologist (Poison Control: 1-800-222-1222 in the US) before it goes into the system. The order would also have to go through your hospital's pharmacy verification process.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like, or give me a different dose."
      }
     ],
